{{- /*
  beads-issues/shared/execution-state-read — read the canonical execution-state
  block from a ticket's `notes`.

  The argument (`.`) is the target bead ID as a plain string.

  Writers: phase workers, loop drivers, Loop until issue complete. Start work
  reads the block and delegates the write to the phase worker it dispatches.
  Readers: every prompt that loads ticket context. Other prompts also write
  unrelated notes content; treat the block as one section, not the whole field.
*/ -}}
- **Read execution state first.** Read recent comments only:
  ```bash
  bd show {{ . }} --long --json | jq -r '.[0].notes // ""' | sed -n '/<!-- mitto:execution-state:v1 -->/,/<!-- \/mitto:execution-state -->/p'
  ```
  If absent, use latest comments and write the block before ending. Fetch referenced
  reports by prefix; do not read full history. Preserve notes outside the marker
  byte-for-byte.
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
